WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.667
Hebrews, Chapter Three.

2
00:00:02.667 --> 00:00:15.733
Wherefore, holy brethren, partakers of the heavenly calling, consider the Apostle and High Priest of our profession, Christ Jesus; Who was faithful to him that appointed him, as also Moses was faithful in all his house.

3
00:00:15.733 --> 00:00:24.000
For this man was counted worthy of more glory than Moses, inasmuch as he who hath builded the house hath more honour than the house.

4
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:30.000
For every house is builded by some man; but he that built all things is God.

5
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:46.933
And Moses verily was faithful in all his house, as a servant, for a testimony of those things which were to be spoken after; But Christ as a son over his own house; whose house are we, if we hold fast the confidence and the rejoicing of the hope firm unto the end.

6
00:00:46.933 --> 00:01:01.467
Wherefore (as the Holy Ghost saith, To day if ye will hear his voice, Harden not your hearts, as in the provocation, in the day of temptation in the wilderness: When your fathers tempted me, proved me, and saw my works forty years.

7
00:01:01.467 --> 00:01:08.800
Wherefore I was grieved with that generation, and said, They do alway err in their heart; and they have not known my ways.

8
00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:20.400
So I sware in my wrath, They shall not enter into my rest.) Take heed, brethren, lest there be in any of you an evil heart of unbelief, in departing from the living God.

9
00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:28.267
But exhort one another daily, while it is called To day; lest any of you be hardened through the deceitfulness of sin.

10
00:01:28.267 --> 00:01:39.733
For we are made partakers of Christ, if we hold the beginning of our confidence stedfast unto the end; While it is said, To day if ye will hear his voice, harden not your hearts, as in the provocation.

11
00:01:39.733 --> 00:01:45.333
For some, when they had heard, did provoke: howbeit not all that came out of Egypt by Moses.

12
00:01:45.333 --> 00:01:48.133
But with whom was he grieved forty years?

13
00:01:48.133 --> 00:01:52.400
was it not with them that had sinned, whose carcases fell in the wilderness?

14
00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:58.267
And to whom sware he that they should not enter into his rest, but to them that believed not?

15
00:01:58.267 --> 00:02:01.333
So we see that they could not enter in because of unbelief.

